  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00TK">Lemma <span data-tag="00TK">10.138.4</span>.</a> A polynomial ring over $R$ is formally smooth over $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose we have a diagram as in Definition <a href="/tag/00TI" data-tag="00TI">10.138.1</a> with $S = R[x_ j; j \in J]$. Then there exists a dotted arrow simply by choosing lifts $a_ j \in A$ of the elements in $A/I$ to which the elements $x_ j$ map to under the top horizontal arrow. 
